# The Wayland surface calls made outside the frame owner (we_wlframe.c) and
# the lost-display places that are meant.  Checked by tests/check-wayland-frame.sh.
#
#   file|rule:function|count|pass|reason
#
# "count" is how many such identifiers the function has: more or fewer fails,
# and a line that matches nothing is stale.  "keep" is a permanent exception.

edit.h|r5:-|1|keep|the declaration of the one lost-display end
we_unix.c|r5:-|1|keep|the definition of the one lost-display end
we_wayland.c|r5:wl_conn_lost|1|keep|the Wayland connection's way into the lost-display end
WeXterm.c|r5:e_x_conn_lost|1|keep|the X connection's way into the lost-display end, which its I/O error handler calls and nothing else
WeXterm.c|r5:WpeXInit|1|keep|the one XSetIOErrorHandler of the editor
we_wayland.c|r1:wl_cursor_apply|3|keep|the cursor's own surface has no xdg role and no configure to answer: attach, damage and commit of a fixed image
